@SmartCraftTask_HostAddress = http://localhost:5087
@warehouseId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@itemId = replace-with-an-id-from-the-list-call

### --- Auth: run ONE of these first. Every other request needs the token. ---

### manager - all four roles, may do anything
POST {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "manager",
  "password": "manager-secret"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### operator - moves stock, reads warehouses, cannot create or delete them (403)
POST {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "operator",
  "password": "operator-secret"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### warehouse-viewer - reads warehouses only; the items endpoints return 403
POST {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "warehouse-viewer",
  "password": "warehouse-viewer-secret"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### stock-viewer - reads stock only; the warehouse endpoints return 403
POST {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "stock-viewer",
  "password": "stock-viewer-secret"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Anonymous: no token at all. Every request below returns 401 until you run one of the above.

### --- Errors and limits ---

### A body that is not JSON: 400, and the deserializer's own wording does not come back with it
POST {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "BAD", oops}

### Run this past the limit (default 10 a minute) to see 429 with Retry-After
POST {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "manager",
  "password": "deliberately-wrong"
}

### --- Health: no token needed, unlike everything else below ---

### Liveness - consults nothing, so it answers even when the database is gone
GET {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/health/live
Accept: application/json

### Readiness - checks the database; 503 while it is unreachable
GET {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/health/ready
Accept: application/json

### --- Warehouses ---

### List warehouses - the first page, 20 at a time unless asked otherwise
GET {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### A small page, so the metadata has something to say. Walk it with pageNumber=2.
GET {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse?pageNumber=1&pageSize=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### A window outside the allowed range - 400, naming the parameter at fault
GET {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse?pageNumber=0&pageSize=5000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### List only the inactive ones
GET {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse?isActive=false
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Fetch a single warehouse - also stores its ETag for the write requests below
GET {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse/{{warehouseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

> {% client.global.set("warehouseEtag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag")); %}

### Create a warehouse
POST {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "STV-01",
  "name": "Stavanger Depot",
  "address": {
    "street": "Havnegata 4",
    "postalCode": "4005",
    "city": "Stavanger",
    "country": "Norway"
  },
  "capacityInPallets": 500
}

### Update a warehouse - run the single-warehouse GET first to fill warehouseEtag.
### Run this twice: the second attempt returns 412, because the first moved the version on.
PUT {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse/{{warehouseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: {{warehouseEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Oslo Central (renovated)",
  "address": {
    "street": "Karl Johans gate 1",
    "postalCode": "0154",
    "city": "Oslo",
    "country": "Norway"
  },
  "capacityInPallets": 1500,
  "isActive": true
}

### Delete a warehouse
DELETE {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse/{{warehouseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: {{warehouseEtag}}

### --- Items (nested under their warehouse) ---

### List the stock lines in a warehouse
GET {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse/{{warehouseId}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Only the lines actually on stock - the filter narrows the total, not just the rows
GET {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse/{{warehouseId}}/items?isOnStock=true&pageSize=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Add a stock line
POST {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse/{{warehouseId}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "PAL-1001",
  "name": "Oak plank 2m",
  "quantity": 12
}

### Fetch a single stock line - stores its ETag, which is its own, not the warehouse's
GET {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse/{{warehouseId}}/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

> {% client.global.set("itemEtag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag")); %}

### Update a stock line (drop quantity to 0 and isOnStock flips in the database)
PUT {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse/{{warehouseId}}/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: {{itemEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Oak plank 2m (discontinued)",
  "quantity": 0
}

### Delete a stock line
DELETE {{SmartCraftTask_HostAddress}}/warehouse/{{warehouseId}}/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: {{itemEtag}}

###
